{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a more concrete storage discrepancy. Batched-log lookup treats every `GetValue` error as “batch absent,” although the Pebble adapter distinguishes a missing key from a read failure. The merge path can then proceed without the existing batch prefix. I’ll investigate whether that can cause a successful write to discard previously stored entries.\n\nThe transport interface also explicitly permits out-of-order delivery, supporting the schedule used in the accepted read-context finding.\n"}}
